+
+    <h2>1. Overview &amp; Core Privacy Principles</h2>
+    <p>
+        <strong>The DevTools Times</strong> is engineered around three foundational privacy commitments:
+    </p>
+    <ul>
+        <li><strong>Privacy by Design &amp; Default:</strong> All optional third-party scripts (analytics and contextual advertising) are disabled by default. Passive visitors can read articles without receiving session cookies or triggering third-party tracking requests.</li>
+        <li><strong>Data Minimization:</strong> We only collect the minimum data strictly necessary to deliver the specific feature you request—such as a pseudonymous username and password when you register or sign in, or article slugs when you actively bookmark an article.</li>
+        <li><strong>User Transparency &amp; Control:</strong> We clearly disclose every category of data processed, its exact purpose, and any external service involved, and allow you to change or revoke optional permissions at any time.</li>
+    </ul>
+
+    <h2>2. Account Registration (Sign Up) &amp; Authentication (Sign In)</h2>
+    <p><strong>What data we collect and why (Purpose Limitation):</strong></p>
+    <ul>
+        <li><strong>Pseudonymous Username:</strong> Used solely to identify your account. We encourage you to choose a pseudonymous handle rather than your real name or email address.</li>
+        <li><strong>Password:</strong> Must be at least 8 characters and include a number. Used exclusively to verify your identity when signing in.</li>
+    </ul>
+    <p><strong>How authentication data is protected:</strong></p>
+    <ul>
+        <li>We do <strong>not</strong> ask for your email address, full name, phone number, physical address, or demographic profile.</li>
+        <li>Authentication requests are sent over HTTPS to our authentication endpoint (<code>us-central1-web-devrel-apps.cloudfunctions.net/times_cdn/api/login</code> and <code>/api/register</code>) with <code>Referrer-Policy: no-referrer</code>, <code>credentials: 'omit'</code>, and <code>Cache-Control: no-store</code>.</li>
+        <li>Plaintext passwords are cleared from component memory immediately upon submission, and authentication tokens are never persisted in <code>localStorage</code>.</li>
+        <li>Third-party analytics and advertising scripts are completely excluded from the Sign In and Sign Up pages, and authentication forms carry <code>data-skip-tracking="true"</code>.</li>
+    </ul>
+
+    <h2>3. Cookies, Local Storage &amp; Session Minimization</h2>
+    <ul>
+        <li><strong>No Passive Session Cookies:</strong> Simply browsing articles on The DevTools Times does not initialize a server session or set a session cookie.</li>
+        <li><strong>On-Demand Reading List Session:</strong> If you actively click the bookmark icon to save an article to your Reading List, an on-demand session stores only the list of bookmarked article slugs (<code>readingList</code>).</li>
+        <li><strong>Privacy Preference Storage:</strong> Your third-party script consent choices are stored locally in your browser under the key <code>dtt_privacy_consent_v1</code> so your preferences are respected across page loads.</li>
+    </ul>
+
+    <h2>4. Third-Party Scripts &amp; Explicit Opt-In Consent</h2>
+    <p>
+        Non-essential third-party scripts are rendered inert (<code>type="text/plain"</code>) in the page layout by default and make zero network connections unless you explicitly opt in:
+    </p>
+    <ul>
+        <li>
+            <strong>Third-Party Interaction Analytics (Opt-In Only):</strong>
+            <code>https://us-central1-web-devrel-apps.cloudfunctions.net/times_cdn/lib/analytics-client.js</code>.
+            When enabled by your explicit consent, this script listens for clicks on links and buttons (excluding elements marked with <code>data-skip-tracking="true"</code>) and sends the clicked element&apos;s tag name, visible text, and timestamp to <code>/times_cdn/api/analytics</code> to measure aggregate reader engagement.
+        </li>
+        <li>
+            <strong>Third-Party Contextual Advertising (Opt-In Only):</strong>
+            <code>https://us-central1-web-devrel-apps.cloudfunctions.net/times_cdn/lib/ad-client.js</code>.
+            When enabled by your explicit consent, this script requests contextual banner and fireplace ad slots from <code>/times_cdn/api/get-ad</code> and renders ad iframes.
+        </li>
+        <li>
+            <strong>Self-Hosted Typography:</strong>
+            Our brand font (<em>Grenze</em>) is self-hosted directly on our origin rather than loaded from third-party font CDNs, preventing your IP address and browser headers from being shared with external font providers.
+        </li>
+    </ul>
+
+    <h2>5. Automated Browser Privacy Signals (GPC &amp; DNT) &amp; Document Headers</h2>
+    <ul>
+        <li><strong>Global Privacy Control (GPC) &amp; Do Not Track (DNT):</strong> We automatically detect <code>navigator.globalPrivacyControl</code> and <code>navigator.doNotTrack</code> signals and default optional third-party analytics and advertising scripts to disabled.</li>
+        <li><strong>Privacy-Enhancing HTTP &amp; Document Headers:</strong> Every page sets a strict <code>Referrer-Policy</code> (<code>no-referrer</code> on authentication pages; <code>strict-origin-when-cross-origin</code> elsewhere), disables speculative DNS prefetching (<code>X-DNS-Prefetch-Control: off</code>), enforces a strict <code>Content-Security-Policy</code>, and applies a <code>Permissions-Policy</code> that blocks camera, microphone, geolocation, and browser ad-profiling APIs (<code>browsing-topics=()</code>, <code>join-ad-interest-group=()</code>, <code>run-ad-auction=()</code>, <code>attribution-reporting=()</code>).</li>
+    </ul>
+
+    <h2>6. Your Privacy Rights &amp; Managing Preferences</h2>
+    <p>
